eing joined.\",\"Choose a strategy before you solve.\",\"Write the answer with a label from the story.\"],independentPractice:[\"Nina plants 2 seeds and then 7 more seeds. Find the total.\",\"A tray has 6 cups and gets 3 more cups. Find the total.\",\"Write your own joining story with total 10.\"],commonPitfalls:[{pitfall:\"Using subtraction because the story has the word after or before.\",repairMove:\"Ask whether the story keeps both amounts together.\"},{pitfall:\"Forgetting the unit in the answer.\",repairMove:\"Copy the object name from the question into the answer sentence.\"}],exitTicket:\"Solve: Sam has 4 shells and finds 6 more. Explain your strategy.\",competencyTags:[\"join story\",\"count on\",\"equation\",\"sum within 10\"]}),spec({topicId:\"us-ca-math-p1-1-h5-model-equation-join-stories-to-10\",knowledgePointCode:\"1-H.5\",strandId:\"1-H\",strandTitle:\"Addition stories within 10\",standardIds:[\"1.OA.A.1\",\"1.OA.C.5\",\"1.OA.D.7\"],difficulty:\"Medium\",estimatedMinutes:20,maisTitle:\"1-H.5 Model-and-Equation Join Stories\",description:\"Represent a joining story with a model and an addition equation, with totals no greater than 10.\",sourceAlignmentSignal:\"IXL 1-H.5 model-and-write addition story skill, paraphrased as a MAIS-owned knowledge point.\",learningGoals:[\"Create a model for each part of a joining story.\",\"Translate the model into an addition equation.\",\"Use the model to check the equation.\"],launch:\"Before writing numbers, show the story with quick circles, tally marks, fingers, or counters.\",conceptExplanation:\"Think of the model as the movie of the story and the equation as the title card. If the model shows 4 shells and 5 more shells joining, the equation should record those same parts and the same whole. When the model and equation agree, your answer has a reason.\",workedExample:{prompt:\"A basket has 4 apples. Then 5 more apples are added. Model the story and write the equation.\",answer:\"4 + 5 = 9\",reasoning:\"Draw 4 counters, then 5 more counters. Counting all counters gives 9, so the matching equation is 4 + 5 = 9.\"},guidedPractice:[\"Draw or build the first part.\",\"Draw or build the second part.\",\"Write the equation in the same order as the model.\"],independentPractice:[\"Model and write an equation for 2 balloons and 6 more balloons.\",\"Model and write an equation for 5 pencils and 4 more pencils.\",\"Create a story, model, and equation for a total of 10.\"],commonPitfalls:[{pitfall:\"The model shows one story but the equation shows another.\",repairMove:\"Point from each group in the model to its number in the equation.\"},{pitfall:\"Writing the plus sign before naming both parts.\",repairMove:\"Say part, part, whole before writing symbols.\"}],exitTicket:\"Draw a model for 6 + 3 and explain how it matches the equation.\",competencyTags:[\"model\",\"addition equation\",\"join story\",\"sum within 10\"]}),spec({topicId:\"us-ca-math-p1-1-h6-equation-match-join-stories-to-10\",knowledgePointCode:\"1-H.6\",strandId:\"1-H\",strandTitle:\"Addition stories within 10\",standardIds:[\"1.OA.A.1\",\"1.OA.D.7\",\"1.OA.D.8\"],difficulty:\"Medium\",estimatedMinutes:20,maisTitle:\"1-H.6 Equation Match for Join Stories\",description:\"Choose or write the addition equation that matches a joining story within 10.\",sourceAlignmentSignal:\"IXL 1-H.6 addition-sentence selection skill, paraphrased as a MAIS-owned knowledge point.\",learningGoals:[\"Identify the two addends in a story.\",\"Match the story to an equation with the correct total.\",\"Use the equals sign to show that both sides name the same amount.\"],launch:\"Read the whole story before choosing an equation. The numbers alone are not enough; the operation must match the action.\",conceptExplanation:\"An equation is true only if it tells the same joining story. Different number sentences may have the same total, but the best match uses the exact two parts from the story. Read the story, point to each part, then choose the equation that makes the picture and words agree.\",workedExample:{prompt:\"A tank has 2 orange fish and 6 silver fish. Which equation matches the total number of fish?\",answer:\"2 + 6 = 8\",reasoning:\"The story joins 2 fish and 6 fish. The total is 8, so 2 + 6 = 8 matches the story.\"},guidedPractice:[\"Cross out equations that use the wrong operation.\",\"Check that both story parts appear in the equation.\",\"Read the equation as a sentence and compare it to the story.\"],independentPractice:[\"Match a story about 1 red cup and 8 blue cups to an equation.\",\"Match a story about 5 small rocks and 5 large rocks to an equation.\",\"Write two true equations and explain which one matches the story order.\"],commonPitfalls:[{pitfall:\"Choosing an equation only because it has the same total.\",repairMove:\"Check that the addends also match the two story parts.\"},{pitfall:\"Treating the equals sign as a signal to calculate instead of a balance.\",repairMove:\"Read equals as 'is the same amount as'.\"}],exitTicket:\"Write the matching equation for a story with 3 red cubes and 4 blue cubes.\",competencyTags:[\"equation match\",\"join story\",\"equals sign\",\"sum within 10\"]}),spec({topicId:\"us-ca-math-p1-1-l1-picture-take-away-stories-to-10\",knowledgePointCode:\"1-L.1\",strandId:\"1-L\",strandTitle:\"Subtraction stories within 10\",standardIds:[\"1.OA.A.1\",\"1.OA.B.4\",\"1.OA.C.6\"],difficulty:\"Low\",estimatedMinutes:18,maisTitle:\"1-L.1 Picture Take-Away Stories to Ten\",description:\"Use a simple picture clue to remove a part and find how many remain within 10.\",sourceAlignmentSignal:\"IXL 1-L.1 subtraction word-problem picture skill, paraphrased as a MAIS-owned knowledge point.\",learningGoals:[\"Identify the starting amount in a picture story.\",\"Identify the part that is taken away.\",\"Count what remains within 10.\"],launch:\"Picture stories for subtraction usually show a starting group and a change. Before solving, name what was there first and what left.\",conceptExplanation:\"A take-away picture has a before and an after. The whole group is there first, then some objects leave, get used, or are crossed out. The answer is the part still left in the picture, not the part that went away.\",workedExample:{prompt:\"A picture shows 9 balloons. Four balloons float away. How many balloons are left?\",answer:\"5\",reasoning:\"Start with 9 balloons and remove 4. Counting back or crossing out 4 leaves 5 balloons.\"},guidedPractice:[\"Box the starting group in the picture.\",\"Cross out or cover the part that leaves.\",\"Count the part that remains.\"],independentPractice:[\"Draw 8 apples and cross out 3. Find how many remain.\",\"Draw 6 cups and remove 2. Find how many remain.\",\"Create a take-away picture with 10 objects.\"],commonPitfalls:[{pitfall:\"Adding the removed part instead of subtracting it.\",repairMove:\"Ask whether the group grows or gets smaller.\"},{pitfall:\"Counting the crossed-out objects as the answer.\",repairMove:\"Point to what is left and count only those objects.\"}],exitTicket:\"Draw a picture for 7 take away 2 and say how many remain.\",competencyTags:[\"picture story\",\"take away\",\"count back\",\"within 10\"]}),spec({topicId:\"us-ca-math-p1-1-l2-picture-story-subtraction-equations\",knowledgePointCode:\"1-L.2\",strandId:\"1-L\",strandTitle:\"Subtraction stories within 10\",standardIds:[\"1.OA.A.1\",\"1.OA.B.4\",\"1.OA.D.7\"],difficulty:\"Low\",estimatedMinutes:18,maisTitle:\"1-L.2 Picture Story Subtraction Equations\",description:\"Turn a picture-based take-away story into a subtraction equation within 10.\",sourceAlignmentSignal:\"IXL 1-L.2 picture-to-subtraction-sentence skill, paraphrased as a MAIS-owned knowledge point.\",learningGoals:[\"Match the starting picture amount to the first number.\",\"Match the removed part to the number after the minus sign.\",\"Check that the equation's result is the amount left.\"],launch:\"Say the picture story with subtraction language: start with, take away, 