,launch:\"Build the whole train first. Then slide away or cover the part that leaves so the remaining part is easy to see.\",conceptExplanation:\"For subtraction, build the whole cube train before anything leaves. When you slide away or cover some cubes, the hidden or moved part shows the take-away action. The cubes still showing are the answer because they are the part left behind.\",workedExample:{prompt:\"A cube train has 10 cubes. Six cubes are covered. How many cubes can you still see?\",answer:\"4\",reasoning:\"Start with 10 cubes and cover 6. The visible part is 4 cubes, so 10 - 6 = 4.\"},guidedPractice:[\"Build the whole train before removing anything.\",\"Count the removed or covered cubes.\",\"Count the visible or remaining cubes to answer.\"],independentPractice:[\"Build 9 cubes and cover 5. Find what remains.\",\"Build 7 cubes and remove 3. Find what remains.\",\"Build a cube-train story with an answer of 2.\"],commonPitfalls:[{pitfall:\"Building only the removed part instead of the starting whole.\",repairMove:\"The train starts with the first number in the story.\"},{pitfall:\"Counting covered cubes as the answer.\",repairMove:\"Choose whether the question asks for covered cubes or visible cubes.\"}],exitTicket:\"Explain how a 9-cube train can show 9 - 4.\",competencyTags:[\"cube train\",\"take away\",\"concrete model\",\"within 10\"]}),spec({topicId:\"us-ca-math-p1-1-l4-take-away-stories-within-10\",knowledgePointCode:\"1-L.4\",strandId:\"1-L\",strandTitle:\"Subtraction stories within 10\",standardIds:[\"1.OA.A.1\",\"1.OA.B.4\",\"1.OA.C.6\"],difficulty:\"Low\",estimatedMinutes:18,maisTitle:\"1-L.4 Take-Away Stories Within Ten\",description:\"Solve a take-away story without relying on a picture, using totals no greater than 10.\",sourceAlignmentSignal:\"IXL 1-L.4 subtraction story skill, paraphrased as a MAIS-owned knowledge point.\",learningGoals:[\"Identify the starting amount and the amount removed.\",\"Choose a subtraction strategy such as counting back, drawing, or using a related addition fact.\",\"Answer with the amount left in the story.\"],launch:\"When a story says some objects are used, given away, eaten, or leave, ask whether the group gets smaller.\",conceptExplanation:\"In a take-away story, the group starts with a full amount and then gets smaller. Words like gave away, ate, used, or left can signal a change, but the story is more important than a keyword. Ask what stayed, because the leftover part is the answer.\",workedExample:{prompt:\"Tara has 7 stickers. She gives 2 stickers to a friend. How many stickers does Tara have left?\",answer:\"5\",reasoning:\"Tara starts with 7 and gives away 2. Count back 2 from 7: 6, 5. Tara has 5 stickers left.\"},guidedPractice:[\"Name the starting amount.\",\"Name the amount that leaves.\",\"Use the story label in the final answer.\"],independentPractice:[\"A box has 8 crayons. Three are used. Find how many are left.\",\"A shelf has 10 books. Four are checked out. Find how many are left.\",\"Write your own take-away story with an answer of 6.\"],commonPitfalls:[{pitfall:\"Using the first two numbers in any order.\",repairMove:\"Keep the starting whole first in a take-away story.\"},{pitfall:\"Stopping the count-back one step too soon.\",repairMove:\"Count the jumps, not just the number words.\"}],exitTicket:\"Solve: 9 markers, 5 are put away. How many are still out?\",competencyTags:[\"take away story\",\"count back\",\"subtraction\",\"within 10\"]}),spec({topicId:\"us-ca-math-p1-1-l5-model-equation-take-away-stories-to-10\",knowledgePointCode:\"1-L.5\",strandId:\"1-L\",strandTitle:\"Subtraction stories within 10\",standardIds:[\"1.OA.A.1\",\"1.OA.B.4\",\"1.OA.C.5\",\"1.OA.D.7\"],difficulty:\"Medium\",estimatedMinutes:20,maisTitle:\"1-L.5 Model-and-Equation Take-Away Stories\",description:\"Represent a take-away story with a model and a subtraction equation within 10.\",sourceAlignmentSignal:\"IXL 1-L.5 model-and-write subtraction story skill, paraphrased as a MAIS-owned knowledge point.\",learningGoals:[\"Model the starting amount before showing the change.\",\"Show the removed part by crossing out, covering, or moving objects.\",\"Write a subtraction equation that matches the model.\"],launch:\"A strong subtraction model shows the whole first. Then it shows exactly what changed.\",conceptExplanation:\"The model is the proof for the subtraction equation. If the model starts with 9 counters and 5 are crossed out, the equation must start with 9 and subtract 5. The leftover counters and the answer in the equation should match.\",workedExample:{prompt:\"Draw 9 counters. Cross out 5 counters. Write an equation for how many counters are left.\",answer:\"9 - 5 = 4\",reasoning:\"The model starts with 9 counters and removes 5. Four counters are not crossed out, so the equation is 9 - 5 = 4.\"},guidedPractice:[\"Draw or build the starting whole.\",\"Show the part taken away without erasing the whole.\",\"Write the equation and point to each part of the model.\"],independentPractice:[\"Model and write an equation for 8 - 6.\",\"Model and write an equation for 10 - 3.\",\"Create a take-away story, model, and equation with an answer of 5.\"],commonPitfalls:[{pitfall:\"Erasing the removed objects so the starting whole is no longer visible.\",repairMove:\"Cross out or cover instead of erasing.\"},{pitfall:\"Writing an equation that does not match the model.\",repairMove:\"Point from the whole, removed part, and leftover part to the equation.\"}],exitTicket:\"Model 6 - 2 and write one sentence explaining the equation.\",competencyTags:[\"model\",\"subtraction equation\",\"take away\",\"within 10\"]}),spec({topicId:\"us-ca-math-p1-1-l6-break-apart-subtraction-equations-to-10\",knowledgePointCode:\"1-L.6\",strandId:\"1-L\",strandTitle:\"Subtraction stories within 10\",standardIds:[\"1.OA.A.1\",\"1.OA.B.4\",\"1.OA.D.7\",\"1.OA.D.8\"],difficulty:\"Medium\",estimatedMinutes:20,maisTitle:\"1-L.6 Break-Apart Subtraction Equations\",description: